cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this model or its outputs, please cite both the accompanying article and this software record."
type: software
title: "Hydrogen truck and refuelling infrastructure rollout model"
abstract: >-
  A Monte Carlo model of heavy-duty fuel-cell truck adoption in California and
  the hydrogen refuelling and production capacity built to serve it. The model
  propagates uncertainty in station and production investment decisions through
  a delivered hydrogen price build-up, a total cost of ownership comparison
  against a diesel baseline, and a social welfare accounting that covers
  climate damages, avoided air-quality damages and public policy expenditure.
  This repository is the code release accompanying the journal article, and
  contains the model, its input configuration, and every script that produces a
  figure or table in the paper.
